{% block user %}Tested {{ adata.uns.get('deseq2_results_meta', {}).get('n_genes', n_vars) }} genes for differential expression between {{ params.get('test_level', 'treated') }} and {{ params.get('reference_level', 'control') }} with DESeq2; positive log2 fold changes are higher in {{ params.get('test_level', 'treated') }}.{% endblock %}

{% block methods %}Differential expression between conditions was assessed on the pseudobulk count matrix with PyDESeq2, the Python implementation of DESeq2 (Love, Huber & Anders 2014 [love_deseq2_2014]). A negative-binomial generalized linear model was fitted with the design {{ params.get('design', '~condition') }}, and the contrast was specified explicitly as ('{{ params.get('condition_col', 'condition') }}', '{{ params.get('test_level', 'treated') }}', '{{ params.get('reference_level', 'control') }}') so that positive log2 fold changes denote higher expression in {{ params.get('test_level', 'treated') }} relative to {{ params.get('reference_level', 'control') }}. P-values were adjusted for multiple testing with the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure.{% endblock %}
